# CLAUDE.md — app/Policies

Authentication (Fortify's session, Sanctum's `auth:sanctum`) is middleware. **Authorization is policies**: every
authenticated action on a record goes through one.

- Register every policy with `Gate::policy(Model::class, ModelPolicy::class)` in `AppServiceProvider::boot()`, one
  visible inventory. Discovery finds only a policy whose name and namespace match its model; a mismatched one silently
  never runs, and every check on that model is denied.
<!-- if:htmx -->
- Every ability is a named method, and the action actually invokes it (`->can()` on the route for writes,
  `Gate::authorize()` otherwise). `@can` in Blade only hides affordances; hiding a button is not authorization.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
- Every ability is a named method, and the action actually invokes it (`->can()` on the route for writes,
  `Gate::authorize()` otherwise). Hiding a button in the frontend is not authorization.
<!-- endif -->
- **Never authorize by a request-supplied identifier.** The subject is `$request->user()`, the record comes from
  route-model binding.
- Authorization lives in ONE place: no `abort(403)` beside a policy call, no ownership `where('user_id', …)` in a
  controller instead of the policy. Scoping a *listing* to the user is a model scope.
- Deny by default: a missing policy method returns false. Prefer 404 over 403 for records the user must not know
  exist.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- Inside a tenant, abilities follow the member's `tenant_user.role` for the current tenant. Another tenant's record
  never reaches a policy: the scope has already answered 404.
<!-- endif -->
- Machine-facing surfaces (API tokens, webhooks) authenticate in middleware and scope from the verified key; a policy
  does not replace that.
<!-- house:end -->
